kri-peshmerga-service-pension-law-2007-5.conditions:
Promotion of officers shall occur upon completing the statutory active time in rank:
- Lieutenant: 3 years;
- First Lieutenant: 3 years;
- Captain: 4 years;
- Major: 4 years;
- Lieutenant Colonel: 4 years;
- Colonel: 4 years;
- Brigadier General: 4 years;
- Major General: 6 years;
- Lieutenant General: 6 years;
- General: By statutory decree of Commander-in-Chief.

kri-peshmerga-service-pension-law-2007-2.conditions:
Peshmerga personnel reach mandatory statutory retirement upon attaining the following ages:
- General and Lieutenant General: 63 years;
- Major General: 60 years;
- Brigadier General: 58 years;
- Colonel: 55 years;
- Lieutenant Colonel: 53 years;
- Major and Captain: 49 years;
- Lieutenant and First Lieutenant: 45 years;
- Technical Corporals to Technical Warrant Officers: 55 years;
- Corporals to Warrant Officers: 50 years;
- Privates to Lance Corporals: 45 years;
2. Military Imams retire at age 60.
3. Certified permanent medical unfitness established by military medical commission.

iraqi-military-procedure-code-2016-2.conditions:
The military judiciary comprises the following judicial bodies:
1. Disciplinary Officer's Court;
2. Military Court;
3. Joint Military Court;
4. Military Court of Cassation.

iraqi-military-procedure-code-2016-3.conditions:
Military trials are classified into two categories:
First: Summary trials conducted before the Disciplinary Officer for minor infractions;
Second: Non-summary trials conducted before competent Military Courts for felonies and major misdemeanors.
